WEBVTT

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.520
Takuya-<i>kun</i>! Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.130
Are you okay?

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.820
One more time...

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.240
Hold it!

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.530
Toyotomi-<i>kun</i>?

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.620
You're late...

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.860
You bastards... will pay!

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.170
We'll get you for this!

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.760
In the end, the good guys always win!

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.530
Are you hurt?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.180
Thank you.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.020
I'm fine.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.350
But Takuya-<i>kun</i> is...

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:31.750
"Episode 3: Tears That Can't Be Stopped"

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:26.790
Those guys went through
a lot of work just to set that up.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:30.080
They were probably trying to
stop tomorrow's briefing from happening.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.610
You okay, Takuya-<i>kun</i>?

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.470
You finally woke up, huh?

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.180
Toyotomi...

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.350
What were you doing there?

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.270
I'm "Useful Flunky A," after all.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:52.770
Don't try to be a hero
and make your mother sad.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.710
Thank you so much for your help today.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.530
Call me anytime.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.280
I'll go wherever you need me.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.040
There was just one time
before when I scolded you, right?

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.300
Do you remember that?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.880
When I came home after getting in a fight.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.270
Yeah. The police said you saved Yuki-<i>kun</i>
from some thugs

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.630
that were bothering him.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.020
Actually, I was really happy.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.640
I thought you were really cool.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.890
You'd really grown up.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:42.460
But now that Kodai-<i>san</i>'s gone,
it's just the two of us.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.030
If something happened to you too...

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.030
I...

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.550
Yeah...

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.120
Please, don't do anything reckless anymore.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.580
Okay...

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.840
Oww...

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:07.470
Morning.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.850
I keep telling you!

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.810
I'm against continuing the construction.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.350
I think we need to find out 
what's going on here now,

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.350
even if it means missing the deadline...

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.940
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.370
Sorry.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.670
No, it's nothing...

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.250
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, knock
before you enter a girl's room.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:35.960
Got it?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.830
Yeah.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.850
Next time you do that, 
I'll punish you, got it?

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.930
Wow, it's great.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.890
Flattery won't get you more allowance.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.680
I mean it!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.440
Here, say "aah."

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.690
Hey! Don't eat my finger, too.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.330
Hey, do you have
anybody you like, Takuya-<i>kun</i>?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.700
Where did that come from?

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.120
Don't change the subject.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.800
I love Hideki Yukawa,
the Nobel prize-winning scientist.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.430
I mean someone you're in love with!

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.930
Okay, Elizabeth Taylor!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.140
Jeez...

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.430
What about you?

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.680
Who do you love the most?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:39.150
Dr. Kodai Arima, of course.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.070
Sorry.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.320
I didn't mean to...

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.450
And there's somebody I love just as much.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.780
He tries to make himself out to
be more of a grown-up than he is,

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.160
but he's a pure-hearted and kind boy.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.660
He says something bad, regrets it,
and immediately apologizes.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.460
He's part of my family,
and I care about him very much.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:06.470
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, what do you
plan to do after you graduate?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.220
Marry somebody.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.600
You'll need to marry into wealth, then.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.750
Don't take that seriously.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.100
What is it you want me to do, Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:21.860
I want you to make a choice you won't regret.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.020
It's not fair when you put it that way.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.360
I mean it.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:29.160
I want you to follow the path you think best.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.280
Look at the time!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.290
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, sorry!

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.500
Can you clean up?

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.330
Sure.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:39.330
See you later.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.220
Morning!

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.430
What the heck happened to you?

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.560
I crashed my moped.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.970
Ow! My whole body aches.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.850
I'm skipping summer school classes
and going to the nurse's office.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.020
I guess today, you've
actually got a good reason...

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.000
Put my name on today's work and turn it in.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.400
I'm a grade lower than you!
I can't do your work!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.900
Just put in something.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.490
What if the teacher comes?

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.330
Pretend to be me!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.080
That's not gonna work!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:17.930
Good luck!

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.600
How are you feeling?

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.770
A lot better.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.420
You, huh?

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.400
She okay?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:48.320
She keeps getting these inexplicable fevers.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.530
There's nothing I can do.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.660
My mom's fever reducer works really well.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.450
You want some?

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.870
Ayumi-<i>san</i>'s?

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.790
No, the one who gave birth to me.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.040
Hmm...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.000
Oh, Kanna-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.790
I think I've seen that accessory before.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.300
Is it the latest thing?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.370
This is not an accessory.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.630
It's the flame of my life.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:21.280
Goodbye.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.730
Strange kid, huh?

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.990
Yup. Even weirder than a teacher
who wears a tight miniskirt to work.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.190
What's weird about this outfit?

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.410
That's not what teachers wear at all!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.700
You're the one who told me
this is what's popular now.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.580
Yeah, but...

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:44.120
You lived outside of Japan
for a long time, right?

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:45.820
You've lost your sense of what's normal here.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.210
Oh, right. Did you see Ichijo-<i>san</i> yet?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.390
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:54.140
She seemed to be looking 
for you a minute ago.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.850
Sorry. I know you're supposed
to be in summer school class.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.040
It's fine. I was cutting and killing
time in the nurse's office instead.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:07.290
I wanted to know what your plans are now.

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.510
Everybody asks me the same thing.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.690
Everybody's worried about you.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:17.460
You had a really rough time
after your dad went missing.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.530
So did you.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.870
Yeah...

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.390
It was hard for me, knowing
he'd never be able to love me back...

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.290
Well, for now, I'm going to graduate.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.230
After that, I don't know.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.680
Does that work for an answer?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.260
What?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.880
You seem a lot more relaxed.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.760
Really?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.020
It's been a long time since
we've had a chance to really talk.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.550
You been busy lately?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:52.350
I'm spending every day going
through your father's research notes.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:01.410
Hey, don't you think something's
changed with Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>, lately?

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.660
Men change.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.410
Take your eye off them for a second,
and they become a totally new person, you know.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.670
It's not like that.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.630
Something seems... different.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:12.890
How?

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:17.220
For example, he threw away
all the furniture in his house.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.290
He's sleeping right on the floor.

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:23.310
Yeah, that's weird, but...

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.640
...not that big a deal.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:30.360
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:36.490
You okay?

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.950
Yeah. Just a migraine.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.660
It happens sometimes.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.200
Be careful, okay?

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.450
He was really weird a while ago...

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.920
Was he dancing around
in his underpants at work?

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.460
I'm being serious!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.920
One day, he was in a bad mood all morning.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.260
Just the phone ringing
was enough to set him off.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.780
That time of the month, huh?

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.220
Sorry.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.700
After that, he became completely
obsessed with his research.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.830
Like something had possessed him.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:16.630
I'll keep an eye on him.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:18.530
Thanks.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.990
If you notice something, tell me right away.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.700
For example, if I said 
I thought he had a gun,

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.910
would you laugh at me?

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.870
It wouldn't surprise me at all.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.150
Anything like that.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.840
"Redial | Hold"

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.090
Hello, this is Takuya.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:45.550
Takuya-<i>kun</i>?

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.640
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.600
What's wrong?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.230
I forgot something at home.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.230
Let me guess. An envelope?

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:53.150
Yup.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:56.730
I hate to ask,
but can you bring it to me at work?

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.610
Sure.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.990
I should hurry, right?

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.360
It's got some important paperwork in it,

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.960
so be careful, okay?

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.080
Stop Geotech!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:09.700
Stop them!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.500
--Please don't push!
--We oppose the construction project!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.500
--You can't all come inside!
--We oppose the construction project!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.540
--We'll make sure everyone gets lunch.
--We oppose it!

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.000
--Thanks for everything...
--Give back our oceans!

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:21.380
--We can't let Geotech get away with this!
--Give them back!

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:23.470
It's our right and duty as citizens!

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.640
I'm not even from Sakaimachi, though.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.010
It's fine, it's fine.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.680
Demonstrations are all about numbers.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:32.810
Stop now!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:33.730
What?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.770
Stop the construction!

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.770
--What's that?
--Stop it!

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.230
You're Arima-<i>kun</i>, right?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.280
The Chief told me what's up.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:46.030
There were a lot of people out there.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:48.280
We're about to hold a public conference.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.900
They should state their complaints there.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.000
Oh, there you are.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.120
What?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.870
That is what happens
when I see something disgusting.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.290
And you got better
after seeing my beautiful face.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.140
Thanks for running that errand for the chief.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.430
I'll give her the documents.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.220
I'll give it to her myself.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:13.570
I don't want germs getting
on these important papers.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.230
Thank you!

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.360
Hey, Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.450
This is a huge help, really.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.280
Chief, it's time.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:27.280
Oh, right.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:29.070
You're busy, huh?

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.630
Okay, I'll see you later.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:53.350
You want to watch the briefing too?

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.350
Briefs? I'm a boxers guy.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.600
The conference.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:02.690
Well, I guess it doesn't matter to
a kid who's not even out of diapers.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:06.820
I'll watch it as a representative
of the good people of the community.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.330
Thanks for your comment before.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:23.180
Are you Dr. Kodai Arima's son?

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.670
Yeah, why?

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.740
You've got your father's eyes.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:32.930
I didn't know my dad was still famous
after he was banned from academia.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.690
I've interviewed him.

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:37.980
He was fascinating--

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:41.480
Chief Arima, the woman in charge
of the Geotechnics Construction Project,

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.280
will now give an explanation.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:49.360
Please begin by looking
at this report on the accidents.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:57.370
The lightning strikes began
to take place right as construction began.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.500
This is the top of Mt. Sankaku.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:05.800
Clouds appeared suddenly, lightning struck,

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.550
and then the clouds quickly disappeared.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:11.260
This was despite the fact
the weather was clear that day,

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:15.720
and the chance of lightning 
was extremely low.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:20.640
We've invited specialists
to come help with this matter.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:25.900
We've introduced safety standards that
are in excess of the ones we normally use.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.280
We've supplied the workers 
with insulated suits,

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:31.240
and are working to prevent
a repeat of the accidents.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.290
Now, we'd like to take questions.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:39.710
Yes, I run a small café on the beach.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:42.670
We've lost a lot of customers lately.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:46.420
Can we ask you to make up
for the funds we've lost?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:50.050
We've gotten permission
from the city to do the construction,

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.970
so we currently have no plans for that.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.680
Personally, I do feel bad 
for your situation...

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.890
Um, you keep saying that
things are "under investigation."

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.100
Is there anything you've actually learned?

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.270
Yes, a little...

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.040
Then tell us!

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:08.780
Um...

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.950
Whenever we try to carry
something off the beach,

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.610
that's when the lightning hits.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.740
Without exception.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:20.250
It's very mysterious,
and we're still trying to figure out why...

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.620
You've angered the god of the sea!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:28.000
These accidents were caused by
your lack of proper preventative measures!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:33.010
We believe the direct cause
to be unpredictable lightning strikes,

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.050
but we're working to introduce new measures--

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:38.260
Then why don't you restart
the construction once you've figured out

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.520
what's causing the lightning?

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.640
That's right!

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.940
It's too dangerous for us to do our jobs!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.810
We don't want to die on the job!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.060
Everyone, listen to me!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:53.030
My husband was wearing an insulated suit,
and he still died in a lightning strike!

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.030
Then what good does it do?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:17:00.240
Insulated suits aren't perfect,
and accidents do happen...

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:18.130
Those idiots don't understand that
we can't be held responsible for the weather.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:24.480
Okay, I'll see you at tonight's recording.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.380
Yes, thank you for the opportunity.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:37.740
Hey, wait!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.290
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.380
That's terrible.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:51.340
Should we postpone the recording a little?

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.670
No, I'm fine.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:56.010
I'll be there right on time.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:17:57.970
Understood.

